      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Given that  $(3{s}^{2}+2s+4)({s}^{2}+3s+2)=3{s}^{4}+a{s}^{3}+b{s}^{2}+cs+8,$ calculate $a+b+c.$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{s}^{2}+2s+4)({s}^{2}+3s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+3s+2)+(2s)({s}^{2}+3s+2)+(4)({s}^{2}+3s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+9{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}+2{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}+4s+4{s}^{2}+12s+8 & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+11{s}^{3}+16{s}^{2}+16s+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=11,$ $b=16,$ and $c=16.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=11+16+16=43.\n$$",
